&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Autonomous Drone Software Engineer to join a swarming programme. As an engineer on a lean, high-impact team, you will have the opportunity to drive development of new features, have a say in architecture and design decisions and have real impact across all the team’s projects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will not be siloed; this role spans the entire autonomy lifecycle, from developing autonomy capabilities to investigating real-world flight-test data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is someone who’s a self-starter, can work independently, can work with ambiguity, can take decisions on their own and not be afraid to drive and push towards getting the project across the finish line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership and drive the development of new features across the autonomy stack and partner integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with hardware engineers, product managers, and external partners to define system requirements and translate them into robust software architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement robust distributed state machines, leader election protocols, and fault-tolerant architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clean, readable and maintainable code while confidently managing complex concurrency and contention scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and run rigorous tests utilizing SITL/HITL simulation environments to validate code prior to physical deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in code reviews, architectural discussions, and technical documentation to elevate the team&#39;s engineering standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act decisively during flight-test investigations, applying strong engineering judgment to physical failure modes and release safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional engineering experience in robotics, embedded systems, or distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep proficiency in modern C++, with practical experience designing, reasoning about, and debugging highly concurrent systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded systems experience working close to hardware on real-time or safety-critical platforms (e.g., avionics, automotive, robotics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong architectural understanding of distributed systems, with the ability to deliberately evaluate and select consensus designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with robust release management, versioned artifacts, and pinned dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4, MAVLink, and related drone software ecosystems is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer at Auterion, you will play a pivotal role in the successful development, integration and deployment of Auterion-powered drone systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will collaborate closely with the production, hardware engineering, and firmware/software teams, as well as operations, ensuring that every platform transitions smoothly from an airframe concept into a fully validated flying robot ready for deployment. You will serve as the primary technical interface for partners, work closely with them to understand their technical requirements, configure and adapt existing solutions, contribute to core software development, and ensure successful implementation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys combining hands-on technical work with customer collaboration and system-level problem solving, bridging the gap between hardware, firmware, and real-world flight performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a highly hands-on environment with evolving system requirements, rapidly iterating across hardware and software integration challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage software releases and perform firmware flashing and configuration using PX4 or adjacent autopilot ecosystems, including sensor calibration, ESC tuning, and system bring-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep avionics and airframe expertise, including autopilot tuning, sensor and payload integration, power systems and airworthiness considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently to troubleshoot integration and flight-readiness issues while collaborating cross-functionally with hardware engineering, firmware/software teams, operations, and QC engineering to escalate complex challenges when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical authority in customer engagements, translating mission requirements into concrete system architectures and demonstrable solutions built on AuterionOS and Skynode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in flight testing activities to validate platform stability, safety, and mission performance, resolving technical issues often directly in the field during customer trials and demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical documentation and continuous improvement of engineering processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed customer and market requirements back into product and engineering teams to influence the roadmap of the Auterion stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Software, Electrical, Mechanical, Aerospace or Robotics Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency in C/C++ and Python: you can read, debug and patch existing code and write small tools and scripts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in Linux environments, including the command line, logs, Docker and basic networking (IP, TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on hardware-software integration: system bring-up, wiring and connectors, and embedded interfaces (UART, CAN, I2C, SPI) at a practical level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured troubleshooting: you can isolate whether a problem is software, hardware, configuration or RF, often under time pressure in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator: you can explain technical issues clearly to customers and operators, and report findings back to engineering in a way they can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel and work on-site with customers, including at test ranges and in field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship (required for security clearance and customer requirements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4 or ArduPilot, MAVLink, QGroundControl or mission planning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UAV flight testing and validation in operational environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with datalinks and radio systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous customer-facing or field engineering role, especially with defense or government customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Ledgy, we’re on a mission to make Europe a powerhouse of entrepreneurship by building a modern, tech-driven equity management and financial reporting platform for private and public companies. In 2026, we aim to be the leading provider for European IPOs and reporting for share-based payments. We are a value-based company with a core focus on being humble, transparent, ambitious and impactful, all in order to delivery the best experience for our customers and end users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to partner with some of the world’s leading investors. New Enterprise Associates led our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://techcrunch.com/2022/09/21/ledgy-a-carta-for-european-startups-to-manage-equity-and-cap-tables-raises-22m-from-nea-sequoia-and-more/&quot;&gt;$22m Series B&lt;/a&gt; round in 2022, with Philip Chopin joining Sequoia’s Luciana Lixandru on our board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We were founded in Switzerland in 2017 and today we operate globally from offices in Zurich and London. We encourage diversity and are an international team coming from 26 different countries and speaking 25 different languages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer on our AI Systems team, you&#39;ll build the AI foundations and product experiences of Ledgy: the Ledgy Agent, the tools and skills it runs on, our MCP server, and the platform capabilities that let other teams embed AI safely in their domains. You&#39;ll collaborate with fellow engineers, product managers, and designers in a new and fast-moving product area where correctness matters as much as speed - our customers need equity data they can trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; We hire remotely across the UK, Spain, Germany, Poland, and Romania. For candidates based in London, we use a hybrid model with 2 days in the office per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team you&#39;ll join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;AI Systems - Develops Ledgy&#39;s AI foundations and product experiences, from AI agents and AI-assisted workflows to the platform capabilities that help other teams embed AI safely in their domains. The team works in a new and evolving product area, balancing rapid iteration with reliable execution, evaluation tooling, and responsible automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Work On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help build the future of how companies manage equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ledgy Agent.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll design and build the system behind our in-app agent, so equity administrators can do through AI what they do manually in the app today. Ledgy Agent takes real actions and runs real analysis on live equity data, like onboarding a stakeholder end to end, and administrators depend on its accuracy and observability. You&#39;ll design the tools, skills, context, and orchestration behind it, and how it decides to handle each request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ledgy MCP.&lt;/strong&gt; Not everyone wants to open Ledgy to get things done. Our MCP server lets customers bring equity into the AI agents and tools they already use. You&#39;ll shape it alongside the in-app agent, so a capability built once works in both places, and you&#39;ll decide what we expose and how we keep it safe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measuring and improving the agent.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll design and build the system we use to measure the agent&#39;s quality and learn from how customers use it: evaluations, tracing, and feedback from real conversations. You decide what &quot;good&quot; means for customers, how we measure it, and how what we learn changes what we build next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling.&lt;/strong&gt; The Ledgy web application, the agent, MCP, and surfaces we haven&#39;t built yet all need the same capabilities. You&#39;ll design the foundations that let us build AI features once and reuse them everywhere, and that let other teams add AI to their domains without compromising correctness. You&#39;ll also design how it runs as usage grows: the backend infrastructure, cost, and latency behind the agent and MCP, and how we keep them reliable and observable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own real parts of this and have a say in where we invest. You&#39;ll also spend time with customers to see how administrators actually use the agent, and use that to decide what to build next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll Thrive in This Role If You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&#39;t worry if you don&#39;t tick every box. These are the things that would make you an especially good fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of experience working as a Software Engineer, with strong TypeScript/Node fundamentals across back end and front end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built and shipped agentic or LLM-based software to production, such as an agent, an assistant, or a chat product, and you&#39;ve been the one running it. You&#39;ve debugged failures in real conversations and kept cost and latency in check as usage and models changed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve designed the agent itself: tools and skills, context and prompt engineering, state, streaming, and the agent loop. You know at least one agent framework or runtime well and can say where it works and where it doesn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You improve these systems with evidence. Evals, regression sets, tracing, and feedback from real usage tell you whether a change helped, and you use them to decide what to do next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You keep up with what the foundation labs and the wider community are learning about building agents. You try new techniques early and judge which ones make our product better and are worth adopting now, and which should wait.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take part in deciding what we build. You read the data, talk to customers, and push for what you think matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work in a TypeScript monorepo: React and Tailwind on the front end, tRPC, Node.js, MongoDB, and Temporal on the back end. It runs on GCP with Kubernetes, managed through Terraform. The agent is currently built on the Vercel AI SDK, and we run an MCP server alongside it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t need to know all of it, but hands-on experience building with LLMs is strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Your Journey Could Look Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First day:&lt;/strong&gt; Get the app running locally and make your first commit. Your onboarding buddy helps you get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First week:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet the engineers, product managers, and designers you&#39;ll work with.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn the agent end to end: its tools, skills, MCP surface, and how we evaluate it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship a few smaller features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First month:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet the wider engineering team and learn how Ledgy works and how customers use it today. This is the background you&#39;ll use for decisions later.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make larger contributions and take a bigger part in code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 3 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive part of a larger piece of work, such as process, tooling, a new product, or new functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product and Design to prove and deepen the value AI adds to the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in architecture and long-term decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;After the first 3 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a bigger role in shaping where the team is heading. Own key parts of our AI platform and decide where we can add the most value for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers and raise the bar. Help teams across Ledgy add AI to what they build, whether that means advising, reviewing, or working alongside them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape Ledgy&#39;s technical direction, for AI and for everything else we build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The interview process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting to know you (45 min):&lt;/strong&gt; Meet with someone from our people team to talk about your experience and to ask questions about the role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live Coding (60 min):&lt;/strong&gt; An equity domain problem to solve collaboratively using your preferred language and IDE. We want to see how you think, so this step does not allow AI. But you can freely look up syntax questions if you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Design (60 min):&lt;/strong&gt; A system design session where you will design an architecture for a problem from the Ledgy domain using a visual tool of your choice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behavioural (45 min):&lt;/strong&gt; Answer behavioural style questions about your experience, using the STAR method - with a PM and EM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture Interview:&lt;/strong&gt; A chance to meet one of our founders and your hiring manager for a 30-minute chat about Ledgy&#39;s mission and values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offer&lt;/strong&gt; 🎉&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Being part of Ledgy means:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recharge and re-energize with flexible working hours, 25 days of vacation, and up to 40 days of remote work from outside your home country.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We make space for your own professional development, with a generous yearly learning &amp;amp; development budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will receive a competitive salary + benefits + equity. All salaries are aligned with competitively benchmarked ranges based on work location and levelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For candidates based in London we use a hybrid work model of 2 days in the office per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Superchat, we&#39;re rebuilding how businesses talk to their customers. The phone call, the contact form, the support ticket: all of it is being replaced by messaging and AI. We&#39;re building the platform that runs underneath.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020, Superchat has become the platform of choice for &lt;strong&gt;10,000+ businesses worldwide&lt;/strong&gt;, from globally recognized brands like Allianz, Auto1, Enpal, Danone, and GASAG to the small businesses, dental practices, and one-person startups that need to look bigger than they are. Today, &lt;strong&gt;millions of messages flow through Superchat every single day&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We started as a unified inbox: one place for every channel a customer might pick, WhatsApp, email, SMS, Instagram. Then ChatGPT happened, and the second chapter began: AI agents that respond across chat, email, and voice at the quality of the best human teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re &lt;strong&gt;100 people&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;profitable&lt;/strong&gt;, and have raised &lt;strong&gt;€18M in funding&lt;/strong&gt; (last round 4.5 years ago, we&#39;ve been growing on our own money since). Headquartered in Berlin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As a Revenue Operations Engineeer you anchor the build end of Revenue Operations - our internal product team whose customers are the GTM functions: Sales, CS, Marketing, and Finance. You build the AI, automation, and data foundations that make these teams faster, smarter, and more scalable, owning the end-to-end delivery of internal tools, integrations, and AI-powered workflows - from problem framing and architecture through launch, adoption, and measurable business impact.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Want&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven GTM Systems Builder.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You bring 3+ years of hands-on experience in RevOps, GTM Engineering, SalesOps, Business Systems, or a comparable B2B SaaS role, and can show production systems you personally built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Native Builder.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ve integrated LLMs into real workflows or tools through APIs and understand how to move beyond prompting into reliable, production-ready use cases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product-Minded Systems Thinker.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You start with the user and business problem, map the relevant process and data dependencies, and choose the simplest scalable solution rather than defaulting to a particular tool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integration &amp;amp; Data Fluent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;re comfortable working with APIs, webhooks, JSON, authentication, data models, and the movement of data between multiple systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Owner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You can take a project from discovery and architecture through building, testing, rollout, documentation, monitoring, and ongoing improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pragmatic Production Engineer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You ship quickly without treating reliability as optional, including appropriate testing, error handling, security, observability, and documentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business-Impact Oriented.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You connect technical work to measurable outcomes such as pipeline, productivity, data quality, speed, cost, or customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear Cross-Functional Communicator.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You can explain technical decisions simply, manage trade-offs, work through ambiguity, and collaborate effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;You are fluent in written and spoken English; German is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious &amp;amp; Self-Directed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You actively experiment with new technologies, learn through building, and share useful findings without chasing novelty for its own sake.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Who We Don’t Want&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;3:1-4:145;22-205&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Uses tools without hands-on depth.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You&#39;ve used CRM and AI tools but lack hands-on experience building automations, configuring systems, or solving operational problems end-to-end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;6:1-7:121;207-378&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Struggles with cross-functional GTM processes.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You find it hard to understand how operational decisions ripple across the wider GTM motion and the business as a whole.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;9:1-10:111;380-530&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weak on the technical fundamentals.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You struggle with APIs, JSON, data models, authentication, debugging, or moving data reliably between systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;12:1-13:137;532-713&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Can&#39;t connect the build to the business.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You can&#39;t explain technical choices clearly, manage trade-offs, influence stakeholders, or connect a build to its wider business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;15:1-16:128;715-886&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Uses AI without shipping anything real.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You use ChatGPT or Claude but can&#39;t point to an LLM-powered workflow, integration, or tool you&#39;ve personally built and shipped.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;18:1-19:169;888-1108&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Builds without thinking about what comes after.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You&#39;ve built isolated automations without considering maintainability, documentation, ownership, failure handling, or how the solution fits into the wider architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Your Day To Day&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building: AI, Automation &amp;amp; Systems (~ 65%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You identify and productionize high-leverage AI use cases across Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, and Finance, including LLM integrations, workflow design, evaluation, guardrails, and monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You design and build lightweight internal applications and interfaces that remove recurring manual work, improve decision-making, and are simple for teams to adopt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build end-to-end workflows using Make, n8n, and custom logic, including business rules, system handoffs, error handling, alerts, and ongoing monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You create clean, maintainable data flows between HubSpot, the data warehouse, billing, support, and other GTM tools using APIs, webhooks, enrichment pipelines, and data activation&lt;/li&gt;
